// A literal vec4 with repeated lanes, written straight to the output
// (t_642eb36e).
//
// The reference compiler does not write the four lanes out verbatim.  It
// packs the DISTINCT values into the const block in first-appearance
// order, zero-fills the rest, and selects with the source swizzle:
//
//     MOVR R0, {0x3f800000(1), 0x3f000000(0.5), 0, 0}.xyxy;
//
// Ours emitted {1, 0.5, 1, 0.5} with an identity swizzle until
// 2026-09-02 - the same pixels, four bytes of const block apart, on a
// shape as common as a constant colour.
//
// The pair matters: the packed block ALONE, read with an identity
// swizzle, would paint (1, 0.5, 0, 0).  A test that checks the const
// block without checking the swizzle would pass on a miscompile.
void main(out float4 oColor : COLOR)
{
    oColor = float4(1.0f, 0.5f, 1.0f, 0.5f);
}
